---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import OAuthButtons from "../components/OAuthButtons.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Register"
  description="Create a free account to personalize garage readings, save history, configure probes, and unlock dashboard tools."
>
  <div class="page-shell page-grid items-start">
    <section class="card animate-zoom-in">
      <h1 class="card-title">Create an account</h1>
      <p class="card-subtitle">
        Free registration unlocks a dashboard tailored to your probes, preferences, and reading history.
      </p>
      <div class="grid gap-4 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Anyone can view live garage temperatures and weather on the home page. Signing up lets you choose what
          appears there, map your own JSON feeds to friendly probe names, and review every snapshot stored for your
          account—see the
          <a class="text-link" href="/about/accounts-and-dashboard">accounts and dashboard guide</a> for the full
          picture.
        </p>
        <p>
          Saved history turns day-to-day readings into trends you can browse in the dashboard. Subscribers can export
          the full record as CSV for seasonal planning, freeze protection, and equipment checks—explained in
          <a class="text-link" href="/about/historical-data">historical data usage</a>. If you are building your own
          probe stack, the
          <a class="text-link" href="/about">about section</a> covers
          <a class="text-link" href="/about/temperature-probes">probe placement</a>,
          <a class="text-link" href="/about/arduino-sketches">Arduino firmware</a>, and the
          <a class="text-link" href="/about/data-flow">path from sensor to screen</a>, including an
          <a class="text-link" href="/about/probe-demo">interactive probe demo</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Not sure whether an account fits your setup, or stuck wiring a feed? Reach out on the
          <a class="text-link" href="/contact">contact page</a>—we help people adapt this project to their own garages
          and workshops. When you are ready, create your account with the form.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6">
        Already have an account?
        <a class="text-link" href="/signin">Sign in</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <form class="form-panel animate-blurred-fade-in" action="/api/auth/register" method="post">
      <div class="form-field">
        <label class="form-label" for="email">Email</label>
        <input class="form-input" type="email" name="email" id="email" required />
      </div>
      <div class="form-field">
        <label class="form-label" for="password">Password</label>
        <input class="form-input" type="password" name="password" id="password" required />
      </div>
      <div class="form-field">
        <div class="cf-turnstile" data-sitekey={import.meta.env.TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY}></div>
      </div>
      <button class="btn-primary" type="submit">Create account</button>
      <OAuthButtons action="/api/auth/signin" />
    </form>
  </div>
</Layout>
